  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), the quadrant from the front and above, fitted with the airliner handles (speed brake, four throttles, flap)",
  "mappingSource": "Honeycomb \"Bravo Throttle Quadrant Configuration for X-Plane 11\" sheet (https://ipadpilotnews-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/07113919/10503-Honeycomb-Bravo-Configuration-X-Plane.pdf): #1-8 AP buttons HDG NAV APR REV ALT VS IAS AUTOPILOT, #9-12 lever 2-5 TOGA, #13/14 AP dial INCR/DECR, #15/16 flap lever down/up, #17-21 AP selector IAS CRS HDG VS ALT, #22/23 trim nose down/up, #24-28 + #33 lever detents, #29 lever 1 TOGA, #30/#48 lever 3/4 commercial TOGA, #31/32 gear up/down, #34-47 switches 1-7; axes X=lever 2, Y=lever 1, Z=lever 5, Rx=lever 4, Ry=lever 3, Rz=lever 6. The catalog matches the sheet.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "Levers are numbered left to right in their slots: lever 1 = SPEED BRAKE handle, levers 2-5 = throttle handles 1-4, lever 6 = FLAP handle (with this handle set). The lever detent buttons are virtual (lever pulled past its stop) and are not placed separately. The seven 2-way switches sit in the row below the AP panel and are hidden behind the levers on this top-down photo; the TOGA buttons of the GA handles (red Go Around) are not fitted here, and the commercial-handle TOGA buttons are not identifiable. The AP buttons HDG, APR and VS are partly covered by the lever stems.",
